# nanopb static-allocation bounds for board.proto.
#
# Command.setpoints decodes through a callback (no static array): the server
# streams setpoints into the sequencer's own table, so a sequence never rides
# in the Envelope union. Request takes submsg_callback for the same reason
# Envelope does (shared.options): the callback has to be installed after the
# oneof union is memset, when the command arm's tag decodes.
board.Request           submsg_callback:true
board.Command.setpoints type:FT_CALLBACK
